WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.697
This view joins employees to departments and sales orders.

00:00:03.697 --> 00:00:06.452
It aggregates orders and sales amount.

00:00:06.452 --> 00:00:09.542
One output row represents one employee.

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:13.617
Because this definition can support several operations reports,

00:00:13.617 --> 00:00:16.857
publishing it as a reusable view is reasonable.

00:00:16.857 --> 00:00:22.092
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:22.092 --> 00:00:28.917
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:28.917 --> 00:00:35.379
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
